From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muthukumar <muthukumardce@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 25 May 2026 02:59:06 +0530
Subject: Blink: NavigatorUAData::Set{Brand,FullVersion}List must clear before
 populating
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Setter methods named "SetX" should replace, not append. The two affected
methods iterate the input and call Add* helpers (which push_back onto
brand_set_ / full_version_list_), but never clear the destination first.

Upstream Chromium never exposes this because each NavigatorUAData
instance is owned by a Document and these methods are invoked exactly
once during construction. The result: 3 brands in, 3 brands out, by
accident.

Electron's session-level fingerprint override path is different.
Session::SetFingerprintOverrides() runs once at tab creation, again on
every profile change, and again on every proxy-timezone re-detection.
Each invocation flows to NavigatorUAData::SetBrandVersionList() on the
same renderer-side instance. Without the clear, brand_set_ accumulates:

  call 1 →  3 entries
  call 2 →  6 entries
  call 3 →  9 entries
  ...
  call N → 3*N entries

The page-visible symptom is navigator.userAgentData.brands returning
something like:

  [
    {brand:"Not(A:Brand", version:"8"},
    {brand:"Chromium",    version:"144"},
    {brand:"Google Chrome", version:"144"},
    {brand:"Not(A:Brand", version:"8"},     // ← duplicate
    {brand:"Chromium",    version:"144"},
    {brand:"Google Chrome", version:"144"},
    ...
  ]

A real Chrome returns each brand exactly once. The duplication is a
high-signal anti-detect-browser tell — iphey.com, pixelscan.net, and
similar fingerprinters key on it (observed: iphey flags the visit as
"Detected anti-detect browser environment" purely on this signal even
when IP, timezone, geolocation, and user-agent string all check out).

Fix: clear brand_set_ / full_version_list_ at the top of each setter,
matching the contract implied by the method name.

The Add* helpers are unchanged — they remain genuine append operations
for callers that want incremental population, just not the ones we own.

diff --git a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_ua_data.cc b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_ua_data.cc
index c0ef0cf964957711622ca3b976d635d8a5cae3bd..e1e9be2f4c250bab4abc499358810121c4800c7b 100644
--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_ua_data.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/frame/navigator_ua_data.cc
@@ -530,6 +530,13 @@ void NavigatorUAData::AddBrandFullVersion(const String& brand,
 
 void NavigatorUAData::SetBrandVersionList(
     const UserAgentBrandList& brand_version_list) {
+  // SetX semantics: replace, not append. Upstream Chromium only calls this
+  // once per NavigatorUAData (created per Document) so the missing clear
+  // is invisible there. In Electron with session-level fingerprint overrides,
+  // we re-apply on every profile/proxy change, and without the clear() the
+  // brand_set_ accumulates 3 new entries per call (anti-fingerprint regression
+  // — iphey + similar pages detect the duplicates and flag as antidetect).
+  brand_set_.clear();
   for (const auto& brand_version : brand_version_list) {
     AddBrandVersion(String::FromUTF8(brand_version.brand),
                     String::FromUTF8(brand_version.version));
@@ -538,6 +545,8 @@ void NavigatorUAData::SetBrandVersionList(
 
 void NavigatorUAData::SetFullVersionList(
     const UserAgentBrandList& full_version_list) {
+  // See SetBrandVersionList above for rationale.
+  full_version_list_.clear();
   for (const auto& brand_version : full_version_list) {
     AddBrandFullVersion(String::FromUTF8(brand_version.brand),
                         String::FromUTF8(brand_version.version));
